{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a120d0dc594df33a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9008\n3\ttitle: Make RHOAI more usable for enterprise teams\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Normal\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\tlinks: []\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## Problem Statement\n12\t\n13\tSeveral strategic accounts have told field teams that RHOAI \"feels hard to use\n14\tat enterprise scale\". Feedback arrived through different channels and has not\n15\tbeen consolidated; the quotes below are representative but partially\n16\tcontradictory. Leadership wants visible usability progress this release.\n17\t\n18\t## High-Level Requirements\n19\t\n20\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n21\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n22\t| HLR-1 | — | Administration should be simpler. One account wants fewer configuration options exposed (\"too many knobs\"), another explicitly wants more fine-grained controls per project. |\n23\t| HLR-2 | — | Onboarding a new data scientist should take \"less than a day\". It is not defined what onboarding includes or where the day is currently spent. |\n24\t| HLR-3 | — | The platform should \"integrate better\" with existing enterprise tooling. No specific tools were named in the consolidated feedback. |\n25\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Publish a whitepaper describing enterprise usability best practices on RHOAI. |\n26\t\n27\t## Affected Components\n28\t\n29\t- Dashboard\n30\t- Notebooks\n31\t\n32\t## Out of Scope\n33\t\n34\tNothing has been explicitly scoped out.\n35\t\n36\t## Open Questions\n37\t\n38\t1. Which accounts' feedback takes precedence when requirements conflict (HLR-1)?\n39\t2. What does \"onboarding\" cover for HLR-2 — cluster access, project setup,\n40\t   first workbench, or first deployed model?\n41\t3. Which enterprise tools does HLR-3 actually mean?\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-825e6e96b89ca063","agent_id":"a2ce99d6c8d9661f6","session_id":"8ed8530c-ec7e