1** here on the strength of \"leadership wants visible usability progress\n  this release\" — not P0 (nothing is release-blocking or an outage) and not P2\n  (the unprioritized HLRs are the point of the strategy, unlike the explicitly\n  P2 whitepaper). This is a judgment call, flagged in Health Warnings.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n| RHAISTRAT-9008-E001 | Resolve the conflicting enterprise requirements for admin configuration | Investigation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9008-E002 | Define data-scientist onboarding scope and locate where the onboarding day is spent | Investigation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9008-E003 | Identify the enterprise tools meant by the integration feedback | Investigation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9008-E004 | Deliver the resolved admin-configuration experience | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9008-E005 | Cut new-data-scientist onboarding time to under a day | Implementation | Workbenches | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9008-E006 | Integrate RHOAI with the identified enterprise tools | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9008-E007 | Publish the enterprise usability best-practices whitepaper | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Docs | P2 |\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[RHAISTRAT-9008-E001<br/>Investigation: admin-config conflict] --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9008-E004<br/>Implementation: admin-config experience]\n    E002[RHAISTRAT-9008-E002<br/>Investigation: onboarding scope/time] --> E005[RHAISTRAT-9008-E005<br/>Implementation: onboarding time]\n    E003[RHAISTRAT-9008-E003<br/>Investigation: enterprise tools] --> E006[RHAISTRAT-9008-E006<br/>Implementation: tool integrations]\n    E004 --> E007[RHAISTRAT-9008-E007<br/>docs-authoring: whitepaper]\n    E005 --> E007\n    E006 --> E007\n```\n\nRoots (E001, E002, E003) are independent investigations that start in\nparallel; each gates exactly one Implementation; the whitepaper is blocked by\nall three Implementations (Rule 11, docs always last).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The HLR-1 conflict (fewer knobs vs. fine-grained controls) cannot be resolved by reading code or docs — it needs the scattered account feedback consolidated and a precedence decision made. The answer rewrites E004's entire scope, so E004 is a true gate (`gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite`, `gated_by=E001`). |\n| E002 → E005 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | What \"onboarding\" covers and where the day is spent determines whether E005 targets workbench startup, console UX, cluster access, or project setup — i.e., which epic exists at all. True gate (`rewrite`), `gated_by=E002`. |\n| E003 → E006 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | No tools are named; until the feedback is consolidated and tools identified, there is nothing to integrate. True gate (`rewrite`), `gated_by=E003`. |\n| E004 → E007 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementations) | The whitepaper describes enterprise usability best practices and must reflect what was actually built; docs are always last. Docs-authoring priority exemption applies (E007 stays P2; no priority inheritance). |\n| E005 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same as above. |\n| E006 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same as above. |\n| E001 ∥ E002 ∥ E003 | Rule 14 analog (independent investigations) | The three unknowns are independent: feedback-conflict resolution, onboarding time analysis, and tool identification neither consume each other's outputs nor share deliverables. They are separate Investigation epics per Step 3 (distinct unknowns, distinct deliverables), run in parallel. E001 and E003 share a feedback-consolidation *method* (both start from the scattered field feedback) and should coordinate, but their deliverables and gated work differ — a decision record vs. a prioritized tool list — so they are not merged. |\n\nNo `konflux-onboarding`, `repo-onboarding`, or `license-validation` epics: both\naffected components are in the platform and Konflux-onboarded per architecture\ncontext. No external-dependry Implementation epics: no upstream PR/RFC is\nrequired by anything stated in the strategy.\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority (strategy) | Priority (assigned) | Epics | Coverage |\n|-----|--------------------|--------------------|-------|----------|\n| HLR-1 — simpler administration (conflicted: fewer knobs vs. more fine-grained controls) | — | P1 | E001 (resolve conflict), E004 (implement resolved direction) | Full — the requirement is inherently two-step: decide, then build |\n| HLR-2 — onboarding a new data scientist in under a day | — | P1 | E002 (define scope, locate time cost), E005 (implement reduction) | Full |\n| HLR-3 — better integration with existing enterprise tooling | — | P1 | E003 (identify tools), E006 (implement integrations) | Full |\n| HLR-4 — publish enterprise usability best-practices whitepaper | P2 | P2 | E007 (docs-authoring) | Full; priority derived from strategy frontmatter `priority: Normal` → P2 |\n\nNo orphaned HLRs. No redundant/overlapping HLRs — HLR-1/2/3/4 describe four\ndistinct capabilities.\n\n## Component Mapping Notes\n\n- `Dashboard` — assigned to E001, E002, E003, E004, E006. The admin-configuration\n  surfaces (per-component feature flags and defaults via `OdhDashboardConfig`),\n  the onboarding entry point (project setup, workbench spawn UI), and any\n  enterprise-tool integration surface through the single-pane console are all\n  Dashboard territory per architecture context. E002's and E003's work spans\n  the whole platform journey, but the Dashboard team is the nearest active\n  owner for both studies.\n- `Notebooks` — assigned to E005. The onboarding milestone ends at \"first\n  workbench\" (open question 2 enumerates it); the workbench lifecycle\n  (notebook-controller, spawn defaults,