is \"partially contradictory\". E001/E003 both begin by\n   consolidating it; if the consolidated corpus contradicts the strategy's\n   framing, the gated implementations will be rewritten (covered by their\n   `gate_failure_impact`).\n6. **Out-of-scope vacuum.** With no explicit exclusions, NFRs (none stated)\n   cannot contradict scope — but the absence of NFRs means the implementation\n   epics carry no performance/reliability bars beyond what their ACs state.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable in the Step 5.5 sense: there is no external dependency with\nuncertain timing (no upstream PR/RFC or vendor deliverable gates anything).\nHowever, the strategy is naturally **phased**: Tier 1 is the three\ninvestigations (risk-reduction — they resolve every unknown before code is\nwritten), Tier 2 is the three gated implementations, and the whitepaper lands\nlast. Each branch (E001→E004→E007-branch, etc.) delivers its findings or value\nindependently of the other two.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35562,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-825e6e96b89ca063","agent_id":"a2ce99d6c8d9661f6","session_id":"8ed8530c-ec7e-4422-9e2a-22ede41c26ec","uuid":"98e80f6e-3b5f-47c5-9d07-681ff2d7173f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:42:23.857Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9008"}
