outcome and rationale in a decision record.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A consolidated feedback inventory exists that lists each contributing\n  account's administration-related ask and its source channel; no known\n  feedback channel is omitted.\n- A decision record states which direction is pursued (simplification,\n  fine-grained per-project controls, or a named hybrid) and why, including the\n  precedence rule applied between conflicting accounts.\n- Both sides of the conflict are explicitly addressed: the decision record\n  states how the losing concern is handled (satisfied by the chosen design,\n  deferred with rationale, or declined with rationale).\n- An implementer reading only the decision record can determine what to build\n  — no further account arbitration is required to start implementation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1** (Administration should be simpler; conflicting account feedback on\n  configuration exposure) — this epic resolves the requirement's internal\n  conflict so it can be implemented at all.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":38654,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-825e6e96b89ca063","agent_id":"a2ce99d6c8d9661f6","session_id":"8ed8530c-ec7e-4422-9e2a-22ede41c26ec","uuid":"d1012ad7-925c-4ddc-a6be-35b63e4d5d06","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:42:42.783Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9008"}
