{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa57f0c2c86e5a0c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E001\n3\ttitle: Resolve the conflicting enterprise requirements for admin configuration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Resolve the conflicting enterprise requirements for admin configuration\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the contradiction inside the strategy's\n30\tadministration requirement: one strategic account wants fewer configuration\n31\toptions exposed (\"too many knobs\") while another explicitly wants more\n32\tfine-grained per-project controls. The enterprise feedback behind both asks is\n33\tscattered across field channels and has never been consolidated. This epic\n34\tconsolidates that feedback, characterizes the conflict, and drives a recorded\n35\tdecision on which direction (simplification, fine-grained controls, or a\n36\thybrid such as progressive disclosure) the platform will pursue — the decision\n37\tthat determines what the admin-configuration implementation builds.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Gather the enterprise-account feedback about administration complexity from\n42\t  all field channels (account teams, support escalations, filed quotes).\n43\t- Produce a consolidated feedback inventory: per account, what was asked, in\n44\t  what terms, through which channel.\n45\t- Characterize the HLR-1 conflict: which accounts want simplification, which\n46\t  want more control, and what each is actually trying to accomplish.\n47\t- Draft resolution options (reduce exposed configuration, add per-project\n48\t  fine-grained controls, or a hybrid that hides complexity behind sensible\n49\t  defaults while keeping advanced control reachable), with the user value and\n50\t  cost of each.\n51\t- Drive the precedence decision with product management and the account teams\n52\t  — including which accounts' feedback takes precedence when requirements\n53\t  conflict — and record the outcome and rationale in a decision record.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A consolidated feedback inventory exists that lists each contributing\n58\t  account's administration-related ask and its source channel; no known\n59\t  feedback channel is omitted.\n60\t- A decision record states which direction is pursued (simplification,\n61\t  fine-grained per-project controls, or a named hybrid) and why, including the\n62\t  precedence rule applied between conflicting accounts.\n63\t- Both sides of the conflict are explicitly addressed: the decision record\n64\t  states how the losing concern is handled (satisfied by the chosen design,\n65\t  deferred with rationale, or declined with rationale).\n66\t- An implementer reading only the decision record can determine what to build\n67\t  — no further account arbitration is required to start implementation.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- **HLR-1** (Administration should be simpler; conflicting account feedback on\n72\t  configuration exposure) — this epic resolves the requirement's internal\n73\t  conflict so it can be implemented at all.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a65da344f1754f2a","agent_id":"a2f6433638117d63b","session_id":"8ed8530c-ec7e-4422-9e2a-22ede41c26ec","uuid":"315be3f0-d1fd-4a8c-a2ed-3a89701de99b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:46:52.661Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa57f0c2c86e5a0c","permission_decision":{"de