** — the defined onboarding scope and\n53\t  the practices that achieve the under-a-day target.\n54\t- **Enterprise tool integration patterns** — how RHOAI connects to the\n55\t  identified enterprise tools and how to configure the integrations.\n56\t- **Measurement guidance** — how enterprise teams can measure their own\n57\t  onboarding and administration friction against the baselines established\n58\t  by the usability investigations.\n59\t\n60\tAdditional scope:\n61\t\n62\t- Draft, technical review, and publication through the Red Hat docs content\n63\t  process.\n64\t- Validate all technical claims against the platform's architecture context\n65\t  and the delivered implementations.\n66\t\n67\t## Acceptance Criteria\n68\t\n69\t- The whitepaper covers every topic in the content outline above.\n70\t- Every technical claim is technically reviewed against the implemented\n71\t  capabilities and the platform's architecture context, with review sign-off\n72\t  recorded.\n73\t- The published whitepaper accurately describes what the platform actually\n74\t  delivers (no aspirational capability presented as shipped).\n75\t- The whitepaper is published through the Red Hat docs content process with\n76\t  its publication location recorded.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- **HLR-4** (Publish a whitepaper describing enterprise usability best\n81\t  practices on RHOAI) — this epic is the requirement's full delivery.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a65da344f1754f2a","agent_id":"a2f6433638117d63b","session_id":"8ed8530c-ec7e-4422-9e2a-22ede41c26ec","uuid":"955821e2-1c6b-46dd-995e-7100418c0bb4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:47:09.240Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a46abf52c767003","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9008 decomposition"}
