on (strategy priority Normal → P2). P2 HLR-4 is covered, not deferred.\n43\t\n44\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n45\tFrontmatter `dependencies` match the summary DAG diagram edge-for-edge:\n46\tE001→E004, E002→E005, E003→E006 (Investigation gates), and E004/E005/E006→E007\n47\t(Rule 11, docs-authoring blocked by all implementations). Arrows run\n48\tdependency → dependent, matching the diagram convention. No cycles, no edges\n49\tto nonexistent epics. No konflux-onboarding, repo-onboarding, or\n50\tlicense-validation epics exist (both components are in-platform and\n51\tKonflux-onboarded per architecture context), so rules 7/8/10 parallelism\n52\tconstraints are vacuously satisfied. The three investigation roots run in\n53\tparallel — nothing serializes naturally-parallel work. Critical path length 3\n54\t(investigation → implementation → whitepaper) is appropriate for a\n55\tmedium-size strategy. Cross-checking epic content for un-captured data\n56\tdependencies: E007's \"Measurement guidance\" draws on investigation baselines,\n57\tbut those reach E007 transitively through the implementation chain each\n58\tinvestigation gates, so no direct edge is missing. E001/E003 coordination is a\n59\tmethod-level note, not an artifact dependency.\n60\t\n61\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n62\tDistinct component/team tuples produce separate epics (Dashboard/RHOAI\n63\tDashboard, Notebooks/Workbenches, Documentation/RHOAI Docs). No epic bundles\n64\tmultiple teams. Implementation epics explicitly restrict documentation work to\n65\tincidental touch-ups (\"no separate content effort\"), and all content\n66\tauthoring is isolated in E007 — no work-product type mixing. No sibling epics\n67\tbuild the same deliverable. Two minor observations (below threshold):\n68\t- E001 and E003 each include consolidating the same unconsolidated\n69\t  field-feedback corpus; E003's scope explicitly coordinates \"rather than\n70\t  duplicating it\" and the deliverables differ (decision record vs. tool