102\t`human_process_gates: -1` (docs content process + technical review). E002's\n103\t`cluster_hardware_dependence: -1` is reasoned as peripheral rather than\n104\tgating — defensible given the measurement requires a live cluster with OAuth\n105\tand CR-backed workbenches.\n106\t\n107\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n108\tEvery epic has testable, deliverable-anchored ACs. Rule-mandated ACs are\n109\tpresent: E004 (a restructuring of capability strategic accounts currently\n110\tuse) carries a rollback/feature-flag AC; E007 (docs-authoring) carries the\n111\ttechnical-review sign-off AC plus a no-aspirational-claims AC; the\n112\timplementation epics each carry a build/test-pipeline-green AC even though no\n113\tkonflux chain exists. E005's under-a-day AC specifies a concrete verification\n114\tmethod (representative run-through or validated measurement equivalent). E006\n115\tincludes a validation-method-recorded AC for real-tool vs. stand-in testing.\n116\tNo AC encodes an external schedule constraint (no lab-turnaround or\n117\treview-cadence soft-ACs found). No epic body references sibling epics by bare\n118\tdraft ID — all cross-references use descriptive names (\"the decision record\n119\tfrom the feedback-consolidation investigation\").\n120\t\n121\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n122\tEvery strategy capability is accounted for: all four HLRs covered, and all\n123\tthree strategy Open Questions are carried into epic scope rather than dropped\n124\t(Q1 conflict precedence → E001's precedence-rule decision record; Q2 onboarding\n125\tstages → E002's stage enumeration and boundary; Q3 unnamed tools → E003's\n126\ttraceable-source shortlist). Both affected components receive implementation\n127\twork (Dashboard via E004/E006, Notebooks via E005). The strategy's missing\n128\tsections (Impacted Teams, Dependencies, ACs, NFRs, Technical Approach) are\n129\tsurfaced as health warnings with derivation notes, not silently ignored. The\n130\tunconsolidated/contrad